##DESCRIPTION
##  Mental Math problems for integer powers.
##ENDDESCRIPTION

##KEYWORDS('mental math', 'integers')

## DBsubject('Arithmetic')
## DBchapter('Integers')
## DBsection('Mental Math')
## Author('Peter Staab')
## Institution('Fitchburg State University')
## Date('5/3/2020')

DOCUMENT();

loadMacros(
    'PGstandard.pl',            'PGML.pl',
    'contextLimitedNumeric.pl', 'PGcourse.pl'
);

Context('LimitedNumeric');

# 3 numbers from 20, 30, ..., 70
@a = random_subset(3, map { 10 * $_ } 2 .. 7);
@b = random_subset(3, map { 10 * $_ } 2 .. 7);

@a1 = map { $_ + 1 } @a;
@b1 = map { $_ - 1 } @b;

BEGIN_PGML
1. Use the identity [` (a+b)^2 = a^2 + 2ab + b^2 `] to calculate then following mentally:

	a) [` [$a1[0]]^2 = `] [___]{Compute($a1[0]**2)}
	b) [` [$a1[1]]^2 = `] [___]{Compute($a1[1]**2)}
	c) [` [$a1[2]]^2 = `] [___]{Compute($a1[2]**2)}

2. And use the identity [` (a-b)^2 = a^2 - 2ab + b^2 `] to calculate then following mentally:

	a) [` [$b1[0]]^2 = `] [___]{Compute($b1[0]**2)}
	b) [` [$b1[1]]^2 = `] [___]{Compute($b1[1]**2)}
	c) [` [$b1[2]]^2 = `] [___]{Compute($b1[2]**2)}

END_PGML

BEGIN_PGML_SOLUTION
1. Note that these all have the form, [`(n+1)^2 = n^2+2n+1 `]. 

    a) [` [$a1[0]]^2 = [$a[0]]^2 + 2\cdot[$a[0]]+1  = [$a[0]**2] + [$a[0]*2] +1 =
            [$a1[0]**2]`]

    b) [` [$a1[1]]^2 = [$a[1]]^2 + 2\cdot[$a[1]]+1  = [$a[1]**2] + [$a[1]*2] +1 =
            [$a1[1]**2]`]

    d) [` [$a1[2]]^2 = [$a[2]]^2 + 2\cdot[$a[2]]+1  = [$a[2]**2] + [$a[2]*2] +1 =
    [$a1[2]**2]`]

2. Note that these all have the form, [`(n-1)^2 = n^2-2n+1 `]. 

    a) [` [$b1[0]]^2 = [$b[0]]^2 - 2\cdot[$b[0]]+1  = [$b[0]**2] - [$a[0]*2] +1 =
            [$b1[0]**2]`]

    b) [` [$b1[1]]^2 = [$b[1]]^2 - 2\cdot[$b[1]]+1  = [$b[1]**2] - [$b[1]*2] +1 =
            [$b1[1]**2]`]

    d) [` [$b1[2]]^2 = [$b[2]]^2 - 2\cdot[$b[2]]+1  = [$b[2]**2] - [$b[2]*2] +1 =
    [$b1[2]**2]`]

END_PGML_SOLUTION
ENDDOCUMENT();
